sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Pharmacy Manager
    participant PS as PS: PharmacyStaff
    participant PP as PP: PharmacyPortal
    actor ADM as Administrator
    participant AD as AD: Admin
    participant AC as AC: AdminConsole
    actor SU as Searcher
    participant C as C: Consumer
    participant CA as CA: ClientApp
    participant API as API: RestApi
    participant AUTH as AUTH: AccessAndAuthentication
    participant ACC as ACC: Account
    participant PH as PH: Pharmacy
    participant VR as VR: VerificationRequest
    participant LD as LD: LicenseDocument
    participant FS as FS: FileStorage
    participant LCA as LCA: LicenseCheckAdapter
    participant DB as DB: RelationalDbGeo
    participant S as S: Search
    participant LST as LST: Listing

    %% ---------- Part 1: the manager registers and submits her license (one-time) ----------
    U->>PS: viewVerificationStatus ()
    PS->>PP: showVerificationStatus ()
    Note over PP: The portal screen also holds the registration form and the license upload
    PP->>API: receiveRequest (registration details, license document)
    API->>API: validateInput ()
    API->>AUTH: authorize (request)
    AUTH-->>API: authorized
    API->>API: routeRequest ()
    API->>PH: register (registration details)
    PH->>DB: save (pharmacy, verificationStatus = pending)
    DB-->>PH: saved
    PH->>VR: submit ()
    VR->>VR: attachDocument ()
    VR->>LD: upload (license document)
    LD->>FS: store (license file)
    FS-->>LD: storagePath
    LD-->>VR: document saved
    VR-->>PH: request is pending
    PH-->>API: registration received (status pending)
    API-->>PP: sendJsonResponse (status pending)
    PP->>PP: showVerificationStatus (pending, listing not live yet)
    PP-->>PS: status shown
    PS-->>U: pending, listing hidden from searchers until verified

    %% ---------- Part 2: the administrator reviews the request ----------
    ADM->>AD: reviewRegistration (requestId)
    AD->>AC: showRequestDetails ()
    AC->>API: receiveRequest (requestId)
    API->>API: validateInput ()
    API->>AUTH: authorize (request)
    AUTH->>ACC: hasPermission (admin role)
    ACC-->>AUTH: allowed
    AUTH-->>API: authorized
    API->>API: routeRequest ()
    API->>VR: checkWithRegistry ()
    VR->>LCA: checkLicense (licenseNumber)
    LCA-->>VR: registry result (license found or not found)
    VR->>LD: download ()
    LD->>FS: retrieve (storagePath)
    FS-->>LD: license file
    LD-->>VR: license document
    VR-->>API: request details, registry result, license document
    API-->>AC: sendJsonResponse (request package)
    AC-->>AD: details displayed
    AD-->>ADM: request details and registry result

    ADM->>AD: checkLicenseManually (requestId)
    AD->>AC: showLicenseDocument ()
    Note over AC: The document is already inside the response above, so no new request is needed
    AC-->>AD: license document displayed
    AD-->>ADM: document to compare with the registry result

    %% ---------- Part 3: the administrator decides ----------
    alt administrator approves
        ADM->>AD: approve (requestId)
        AD->>AC: recordDecision (approved)
        AC->>API: receiveRequest (requestId, decision approved)
        API->>AUTH: authorize (request)
        AUTH-->>API: authorized (admin role)
        API->>VR: markVerified ()
        VR->>PH: updateProfile (verificationStatus = verified)
        PH->>DB: save (pharmacy)
        DB-->>PH: saved
        PH-->>VR: profile updated
        VR-->>API: request verified
    else administrator rejects
        ADM->>AD: reject (requestId, reason)
        AD->>AC: recordDecision (rejected)
        AC->>API: receiveRequest (requestId, decision rejected, reason)
        API->>AUTH: authorize (request)
        AUTH-->>API: authorized (admin role)
        API->>VR: markRejected (reason)
        VR->>PH: updateProfile (verificationStatus = rejected)
        PH->>DB: save (pharmacy)
        DB-->>PH: saved
        PH-->>VR: profile updated
        VR-->>API: request rejected
    end
    API-->>AC: sendJsonResponse (decision saved)
    AC-->>AD: decision recorded
    AD-->>ADM: decision confirmed

    %% ---------- Part 4: the manager sees the new status ----------
    U->>PS: viewVerificationStatus ()
    PS->>PP: showVerificationStatus ()
    PP->>API: receiveRequest (pharmacyId)
    API->>API: validateInput ()
    API->>AUTH: authorize (request)
    AUTH->>AUTH: checkPharmacyScope ()
    AUTH->>ACC: canAccessPharmacy (pharmacyId)
    ACC-->>AUTH: yes (own pharmacy)
    AUTH-->>API: authorized
    API->>API: routeRequest ()
    API->>PH: isVerified ()
    PH-->>API: verified or rejected
    API-->>PP: sendJsonResponse (verification status)
    PP->>PP: showVerificationStatus (verified and live, or rejected)
    PP-->>PS: status shown
    PS-->>U: verified and live, or rejected

    %% ---------- Part 5: a searcher sees only verified pharmacies, with the badge ----------
    SU->>C: searchMedicine (medicineName)
    C->>CA: showSearchForm ()
    CA->>API: receiveRequest (medicineName, currentLocation)
    API->>AUTH: authorize (request)
    AUTH-->>API: authorized (consumers can search without logging in)
    API->>S: matchProduct (medicineName, origin)
    Note over S: Product matching, origin lookup and finding listings work exactly as in the search diagram from the first sequence diagram
    loop for each listing found
        S->>LST: isInStock ()
        LST->>PH: isVisibleInSearch ()
        PH->>PH: isVerified ()
        alt pharmacy is verified
            PH-->>LST: visible (pharmacy name, verified)
        else pharmacy is not verified
            PH-->>LST: hidden
        end
        LST-->>S: stock status, price, pharmacy info
    end
    S->>S: filterVerifiedOnly ()
    S-->>API: results from verified pharmacies only
    API-->>CA: sendJsonResponse (results)
    CA->>CA: showResults (pharmacy name, stock status, price, presentation)
    CA->>CA: showVerifiedBadge ()
    CA-->>C: results displayed with verified badge
    C-->>SU: nearby verified pharmacies